acking-wide mb-3\",\"children\":\"Popular Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-dog/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"How to Name Your Dog\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-cat/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"How to Name Your Cat\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/guide/japanese-animal-names/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Japanese Animal Names\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/guide/mythological-animal-names/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Mythological Names\"}]}]]}]]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-3\",\"children\":\"Latest Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/top-100-dog-names-2024/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Top 100 Dog Names\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/unique-cat-names-stand-out/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Unique Cat Names\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/mythological-animal-names/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Mythological Names\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/norse-viking-animal-names/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-white transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Norse Viking Names\"}]}]]}]]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 pt-6 border-t border-gray-800 text-center text-xs text-gray-500\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"© \",2026,\" Animal Name Generator. All rights reserved.\"]}]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L14\",null,[\"$\",\"$L15\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@17\"}]}]]}]\n18:[]\n10:\"$W18\"\n11:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"children\":\"$L1a\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L1c\"}]}]}],null]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0_novvjei_gxi.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n1d:T308e,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Artistic and Creative Pet Names: 140+ Inspired Ideas from Art, Music, and Literature\",\"description\":\"140+ artistic pet names from famous painters, composers, writers, and creative movements. Beautiful, cultured names for pets with artistic souls and creative spirits.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-08\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/artistic-creative-pet-names-inspired/\"},\"wordCount\":1663,\"articleBody\":\"Table of Contents 1. The Beauty of Artistic Names | 2. Painter and Visual Artist Names | 3. Composer and Musician Names | 4. Writer and Poet Names | 5. Dance and Theater Names | 6. Creative Movement and Style Names The Beauty of Artistic Pet Names Art, music, literature, and dance represent humanity's highest creative achievements. Naming a pet after a great artist, composer, writer, or creative movement connects your companion to centuries of human culture and imagination. An artistic pet name carries sophistication and personal meaning. It says something about your values, your cultural interests, and the way you see your pet not merely as an animal but as a muse, a companion whose presence inspires the same joy that great art provides. A cat named Frida carries Frida Kahlo's fierce creativity. A dog named Mozart carries musical genius in their very name. Artistic names also tend to be distinctive and memorable. While Bella and Max occupy every dog park, a pet named Matisse or Calliope stands out immediately. These names reward explanation and spark genuine conversation. This guide explores 140+ artistic pet names drawn from painting, music, literature, dance, and creative movements throughout history. Each name has been chosen for its cultural significance, phonetic beauty, and genuine suitability as a daily-use pet name. Whether your companion is a dramatic husky who deserves an opera name or a contemplative cat who channels painterly energy, the arts provide a name as unique as your pet. Painter and Visual Artist Pet Names The history of painting provides an extraordinary vocabulary of artist names that double as beautiful pet names. Frida carries the energy of Frida Kahlo, the Mexican painter whose self-portraits and works celebrating Mexican culture and the female experience made her one of the most significant artists of the 20th century. For pets with distinctive markings or strong personalities, Frida provides a name rich with creative and feminist power. Monet, the French Impressionist whose water lilies and garden scenes defined an artistic movement, provides a name suggesting beauty, light, and gentleness. More painter names: Picasso for the pet who sees the world differently, perhaps with slightly asymmetrical features that capture the cubist spirit. Matisse brings French colorist elegance. Dali evokes surrealist imagination for truly unusual pets. O'Keeffe channels the American Southwest and bold floral imagery. Rembrandt suggests old master gravitas. Van Gogh, perhaps shortened to Vince, carries passionate, starry-night creative energy. Warhol brings pop art cool. Basquiat captures raw, energetic, street-to-gallery creative power. These painter names connect pets to the visual artists who taught humanity to see the world differently, transforming everyday scenes into transcendent beauty. Composer and Musician Pet Names Music provides pet names that carry the beauty of sound itself. Mozart, perhaps the most famous composer in Western history, provides a name suggesting genius, playfulness, and divine musical talent. For the pet whose vocalizations seem almost musical, Mozart captures that quality perfectly. Beethoven carries the weight of symphonic power and the triumph of creativity over adversity. A deaf composer creating some of humanity's greatest music provides inspiration for pets who overcome challenges. Bach suggests mathematical precision and baroque beauty. More composer and musician names: Chopin for romantic, poetic pets with delicate sensibilities. Debussy brings impressionist musical beauty. Vivaldi captures the energy of The Four Seasons and baroque Venice. Ella honors Ella Fitzgerald, the First Lady of Song. Miles references Miles Davis and cool jazz sophistication. Bowie captures David Bowie's shape-shifting creative genius. Prince carries the Purple One's musical royalty. Stevie, for Stevie Wonder or Stevie Nicks, bridges musical genres. Lennon and McCartney provide Beatle-inspired naming. These musical names fill daily life with the resonance of great music, transforming every call of your pet's name into an echo of humanity's greatest artistic achievement. Writer and Poet Pet Names Literature provides pet names that carry the beauty of language and storytelling. Shakespeare, perhaps shortened to Will or Shakes, brings the weight of the English language's greatest writer to pet naming. For pets with dramatic personalities who seem to perform their emotions, a Shakespearean name captures that theatrical quality. Austen, for Jane Austen, brings wit, social observation, and romantic sensibility. For the pet who seems to understand social dynamics better than anyone, Austen provides literary sophistication. Poet names carry particular beauty: Shelley bridges Romantic poetry and gender-neutral naming. Byron carries dark, brooding Romantic energy for pets with dramatic flair. Keats suggests beauty, mortality, and the transcendent power of art. Dickinson, for Emily Dickinson, brings reclusive genius and precise observation of nature. For 20th century literary giants: Hemingway suggests rugged adventure and concise power. Fitzgerald captures Jazz Age glamour. Woolf brings modernist stream-of-consciousness depth. Angelou honors Maya Angelou's poetic wisdom and civil rights legacy. These literary names connect pets to the writers who explored the human condition through language, giving companions names wrapped in centuries of stories, poems, and the eternal human effort to capture experience in words. Dance and Theater Pet Names Dance and theater provide pet names rich with movement, drama, and performance energy. Ballet terminology provides especially elegant naming: Pirouette describes the spinning turn. Plié, the graceful knee bend, works for pets who bow or stretch elegantly. Arabesque suggests extended, balanced beauty. Tutu references the iconic ballet costume with playful charm. For pets with particularly graceful movements, these ballet names capture their physical elegance in a single word. Theater names carry dramatic energy: Thespian, perhaps shortened to Thes, references the tradition of acting itself. Drama works for the pet who turns every minor inconvenience into a theatrical production. Stage suggests performance and presence. Curtain references the theater's central mechanism. Broadway brings New York theatrical energy. Encore describes the pet who always wants one more treat, one more walk, one more moment of attention. Shakespeare bridges literary and theatrical naming. For dance beyond ballet: Tango captures passionate partnership. Salsa brings Latin dance energy. These performance names celebrate the dramatic, expressive, and beautifully choreographed aspects of pet personality that make every day with an animal feel like a performance worth applauding. Art Movements and Creative Style Names Art movements and creative styles provide distinctive pet names that carry entire philosophies of artistic expression. Baroque suggests ornate, dramatic, emotionally intense beauty. For the pet who enters rooms like a cathedral organ chord, Baroque captures that energy. Rococo brings lighter, more playful 18th century elegance. Impressionist, perhaps shortened to Impression, suggests the beauty of light and moment. Cubist, shortened to Cube, works for square-headed, solidly built pets. Surreal works for the truly unusual companion who defies categorization. More art movement names: Dada captures the absurdist, anti-art movement of the early 20th century. Perfect for pets who seem to question the very concept of obedience. Art Deco brings 1920s geometric glamour. Minimalist, shortened to Mini or Mal, works for pets who prefer simplicity. Abstract describes pets whose behavior defies logical explanation. Color Field references the large-canvas color-focused movement and provides Color as a possible shortened form. Renaissance captures the rebirth of classical learning and art. These art movement names give pets identities wrapped in the history of human creativity, celebrating the ever-evolving human effort to understand and express beauty. Architecture and Design Pet Names Architecture provides pet names that carry the beauty of built form and human creative achievement. Column references the classical orders that support great buildings, shortened to Col for a sturdy, reliable companion. Arch describes the curved structural element, suggesting both strength and grace. Dome captures the sweeping, heavenly quality of great domed spaces. Gable references the triangular roof element for pets who peak at everything. Facade, perhaps shortened to Fade, describes the face of a building and works for particularly photogenic pets. Famous architects provide naming as distinctive as their buildings: Frank (Lloyd Wright) carries organic architecture and American design genius. Zaha (Hadid) honors the Iraqi-British architect whose flowing, futuristic designs transformed contemporary architecture. Gaudi references the Catalan modernist whose Sagrada Familia remains unfinished after more than a century. I.M. (Pei) provides initials-as-name from the architect of the Louvre Pyramid. These architectural names celebrate the art of building, connecting pets to humanity's most visible and enduring creative achievements. Fashion and Design Icon Pet Names Fashion provides pet names that carry elegance, style, and cultural sophistication. Coco (Chanel) remains one of the most popular fashion-inspired pet names, carrying French elegance and the timeless appeal of the little black dress. For the pet who always appears impeccably groomed, Coco provides fashion royalty. Versace brings Italian luxury and bold pattern. Armani suggests understated Italian elegance. Gucci carries recognizable luxury branding. Prada evokes Milan sophistication. Explore our name generators for {arapaima}, {alpaca}, {amazon-parrot}, {alpaca-huacaya}, and {alpine-salamander} to find the perfect name for your companion. For more distinctive fashion naming: Dior brings French haute couture. Givenchy channels Audrey Hepburn elegance. McQueen honors Alexander McQueen's dramatic, boundary-pushing creativity. Yves (Saint Laurent) provides simple elegance. These fashion names celebrate the designers who shaped how we present ourselves to the world, giving pets identities wrapped in the artistry of clothing, accessory, and personal style. A pet named Coco or Armani carries a touch of runway elegance into every dog park visit and veterinary waiting room. 🌍 A Real-World Naming Story Sometimes the best names come from the most unexpected places. Take Elena, a wildlife photographer who spent months observing mongolian-wild-horses in their natural habitat. When she finally adopted one as a pet, the name came naturally: 'Obsidian' — inspired by the volcanic rock formations where she first encountered the species. 'I didn't choose the name,' Elena recalls. 'The experience chose it for me.' This story illustrates a deeper naming principle: the most meaningful names aren't always found in lists or generators. They emerge from lived experience — a memorable trip, a childhood memory, a favorite artwork, a piece of music that moved you. These names carry stories, and stories are what transform a simple label into a lifelong connection with your animal companion. Discover more naming inspiration: {sperm-whale}, {polish-lowland-sheepdog}, {northern-flicker}, {foxface-rabbitfish}, {english-springer-spaniel}, and hundreds more animal name generators at BestAnimalNames.com.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-artistic-creative-pet-names-inspired.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}14:[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1d\"}}],\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\",\"$L21\"]\n22:Ta3a,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the most popular artist names for pets?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Frida, Monet, Picasso, Dali, and Matisse are the most popular visual artist pet names. For musicians, Mozart, Beethoven, Bowie, and Ella dominate. These names carry recognizable cultural significance while remaining phonetically appealing for daily pet use.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do artistic names work for any pet species?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Absolutely. Artistic names transcend species. A hamster named Frida or a rabbit named Mozart carries the same cultural weight as a dog or cat with the same name. The perceived personality of different species even enhances certain names. Cats especially suit painter names for their natural grace.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Should I choose an artist name based on my pet's appearance or personality?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Both approaches work. Appearance matching like naming a blue-grey dog Picasso after his Blue Period creates visual-artistic connection. Personality matching like naming a dramatic pet Calliope for the dramatic muse rewards knowing your pet. The best artistic names often combine both elements.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I use lesser-known artists for truly unique pet names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Lesser-known artists provide the most unique names. Artemisia (Gentileschi, Baroque painter), Hilma (af Klint, abstract pioneer), and Basquiat (Jean-Michel, neo-expressionist) reward cultural knowledge while ensuring your pet's name stands out at every veterinary visit and dog park introduction.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What artistic names work well for pairs of pets?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Artistic pairs celebrate creative partnerships: Frida and Diego, John and Yoko, Gertrude and Alice, Pablo and Dora, Jackson and Lee. Famous artistic couples and collaborations provide meaningful paired naming that tells a story about creative partnership through your pets' companionship.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I choose between a music-inspired name and a visual-art-inspired name?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Consider your pet's personality. Visual, observant pets who study their surroundings suit painter or sculptor names (Monet, Frida, Brancusi). Vocal, sound-responsive pets pair naturally with musical names (Jazz, Lyric, Cadence). Let your pet's natural tendencies guide you toward the right artistic discipline.\"}}]}1e:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$22\"}}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Artistic and Creative Pet Names: 140+ Inspired Ideas from Art, Music, and Literature\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/artistic-creative-pet-names-inspired/\\\"}]}\"}}]\n20:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500 flex gap-1 flex-wrap\",\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 font-medium\",\"children\":\"Artistic and Creative Pet Names: 140+ Inspired Ideas from Art, Music, and Literature\"}]]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-6xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"🎨\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Creative Names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"2026-06-08\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"By BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Artistic and Creative Pet Names: 140+ Inspired Ideas from Art, Music, and Literature\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"140+ artistic pet names from famous painters, composers, writers, and creative movements. Beautiful, cultured names for pets with artistic souls and creative spirits.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mt-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"artistic pet names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"artistic pet names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"artist names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"artist names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"composer names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"composer names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"literary names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"literary names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"creative names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"creative names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"1. The Beauty of Artistic Names | 2. Painter and Visual Artist Names | 3. Composer and Musician Names | 4. Writer and Poet Names | 5. Dance and Theater Names | 6. Creative Movement and Style Names\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"The Beauty of Artistic Pet Names\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Art, music, literature, and dance represent humanity's highest creative achievements. Naming a pet after a great artist, composer, writer, or creative movement connects your companion to centuries of human culture and imagination. An artistic pet name carries sophistication and personal meaning. It says something about your values, your cultural interests, and the way you see your pet not merely as an animal but as a muse, a companion whose presence inspires the same joy that great art provides. A cat named Frida carries Frida Kahlo's fierce creativity. A dog named Mozart carries musical genius in their very name.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Artistic names also tend to be distinctive and memorable. While Bella and Max occupy every dog park, a pet named Matisse or Calliope stands out immediately. These names reward explanation and spark genuine conversation. This guide explores 140+ artistic pet names drawn from painting, music, literature, dance, and creative movements throughout history. Each name has been chosen for its cultural significance, phonetic beauty, and genuine suitability as a daily-use pet name. Whether your companion is a dramatic husky who deserves an opera name or a contemplative cat who channels painterly energy, the arts provide a name as unique as your pet.\"]}],\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\",\"$L37\",\"$L38\",\"$L39\",\"$L3a\",\"$L3b\",\"$L3c\"]}],\"$L3d\",\"$L3e\",\"$L3f\",\"$L40\",\"$L41\",\"$L42\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Painter and Visual Artist Pet Names\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The history of painting provides an extraordinary vocabulary of artist names that double as beautiful pet names. Frida carries the energy of Frida Kahlo, the Mexican painter whose self-portraits and works celebrating Mexican culture and the female experience made her one of the most significant artists of the 20th century. For pets with distinctive markings or strong personalities, Frida provides a name rich with creative and feminist power. Monet, the French Impressionist whose water lilies and garden scenes defined an artistic movement, provides a name suggesting beauty, light, and gentleness.\"]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"More painter names: Picasso for the pet who sees the world differently, perhaps with slightly asymmetrical features that capture the cubist spirit. Matisse brings French colorist elegance. Dali evokes surrealist imagination for truly unusual pets. O'Keeffe channels the American Southwest and bold floral imagery. Rembrandt suggests old master gravitas. Van Gogh, perhaps shortened to Vince, carries passionate, starry-night creative energy. Warhol brings pop art cool. Basquiat captures raw, energetic, street-to-gallery creative power. These painter names connect pets to the visual artists who taught humanity to see the world differently, transforming everyday scenes into transcendent beauty.\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Composer and Musician Pet Names\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Music provides pet names that carry the beauty of sound itself. Mozart, perhaps the most famous composer in Western history, provides a name suggesting genius, playfulness, and divine musical talent. For the pet whose vocalizations seem almost musical, Mozart captures that quality perfectly. Beethoven carries the weight of symphonic power and the triumph of creativity over adversity. A deaf composer creating some of humanity's greatest music provides inspiration for pets who overcome challenges. Bach suggests mathematical precision and baroque beauty.\"]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"More composer and musician names: Chopin for romantic, poetic pets with delicate sensibilities. Debussy brings impressionist musical beauty. Vivaldi captures the energy of The Four Seasons and baroque Venice. Ella honors Ella Fitzgerald, the First Lady of Song. Miles references Miles Davis and cool jazz sophistication. Bowie captures David Bowie's shape-shifting creative genius. Prince carries the Purple One's musical royalty. Stevie, for Stevie Wonder or Stevie Nicks, bridges musical genres. Lennon and McCartney provide Beatle-inspired naming. These musical names fill daily life with the resonance of great music, transforming every call of your pet's name into an echo of humanity's greatest artistic achievement.\"]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Writer and Poet Pet Names\"]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Literature provides pet names that carry the beauty of language and storytelling. Shakespeare, perhaps shortened to Will or Shakes, brings the weight of the English language's greatest writer to pet naming. For pets with dramatic personalities who seem to perform their emotions, a Shakespearean name captures that theatrical quality. Austen, for Jane Austen, brings wit, social observation, and romantic sensibility. For the pet who seems to understand social dynamics better than anyone, Austen provides literary sophistication.\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Poet names carry particular beauty: Shelley bridges Romantic poetry and gender-neutral naming. Byron carries dark, brooding Romantic energy for pets with dramatic flair. Keats suggests beauty, mortality, and the transcendent power of art. Dickinson, for Emily Dickinson, brings reclusive genius and precise observation of nature. For 20th century literary giants: Hemingway suggests rugged adventure and concise power. Fitzgerald captures Jazz Age glamour. Woolf brings modernist stream-of-consciousness depth. Angelou honors Maya Angelou's poetic wisdom and civil rights legacy. These literary names connect pets to the writers who explored the human condition through language, giving companions names wrapped in centuries of stories, poems, and the eternal human effort to capture experience in words.\"]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Dance and Theater Pet Names\"]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Dance and theater provide pet names rich with movement, drama, and performance energy. Ballet terminology provides especially elegant naming: Pirouette describes the spinning turn. Plié, the graceful knee bend, works for pets who bow or stretch elegantly. Arabesque suggests extended, balanced beauty. Tutu references the iconic ballet costume with playful charm. For pets with particularly graceful movements, these ballet names capture their physical elegance in a single word.\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Theater names carry dramatic energy: Thespian, perhaps shortened to Thes, references the tradition of acting itself. Drama works for the pet who turns every minor inconvenience into a theatrical production. Stage suggests performance and presence. Curtain references the theater's central mechanism. Broadway brings New York theatrical energy. Encore describes the pet who always wants one more treat, one more walk, one more moment of attention. Shakespeare bridges literary and theatrical naming. For dance beyond ballet: Tango captures passionate partnership. Salsa brings Latin dance energy. These performance names celebrate the dramatic, expressive, and beautifully choreographed aspects of pet personality that make every day with an animal feel like a performance worth applauding.\"]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Art Movements and Creative Style Names\"]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Art movements and creative styles provide distinctive pet names that carry entire philosophies of artistic expression. Baroque suggests ornate, dramatic, emotionally intense beauty. For the pet who enters rooms like a cathedral organ chord, Baroque captures that energy. Rococo brings lighter, more playful 18th century elegance. Impressionist, perhaps shortened to Impression, suggests the beauty of light and moment. Cubist, shortened to Cube, works for square-headed, solidly built pets. Surreal works for the truly unusual companion who defies categorization.\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"More art movement names: Dada captures the absurdist, anti-art movement of the early 20th century. Perfect for pets who seem to question the very concept of obedience. Art Deco brings 1920s geometric glamour. Minimalist, shortened to Mini or Mal, works for pets who prefer simplicity. Abstract describes pets whose behavior defies logical explanation. Color Field references the large-canvas color-focused movement and provides Color as a possible shortened form. Renaissance captures the rebirth of classical learning and art. These art movement names give pets identities wrapped in the history of human creativity, celebrating the ever-evolving human effort to understand and express beauty.\"]}]\n32:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Architecture and Design Pet Names\"]}]\n33:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Architecture provides pet names that carry the beauty of built form and human creative achievement. Column references the classical orders that support great buildings, shortened to Col for a sturdy, reliable companion. Arch describes the curved structural element, suggesting both strength and grace. Dome captures the sweeping, heavenly quality of great domed spaces. Gable references the triangular roof element for pets who peak at everything. Facade, perhaps shortened to Fade, describes the face of a building and works for particularly photogenic pets.\"]}]\n34:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Famous architects provide naming as distinctive as their buildings: Frank (Lloyd Wright) carries organic architecture and American design genius. Zaha (Hadid) honors the Iraqi-British architect whose flowing, futuristic designs transformed contemporary architecture. Gaudi references the Catalan modernist whose Sagrada Familia remains unfinished after more than a century. I.M. (Pei) provides initials-as-name from the architect of the Louvre Pyramid. These architectural names celebrate the art of building, connecting pets to humanity's most visible and enduring creative achievements.\"]}]\n35:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Fashion and Design Icon Pet Names\"]}]\n36:[\"$\",\"p\",\"24\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Fashion provides pet names that carry elegance, style, and cultural sophistication. Coco (Chanel) remains one of the most popular fashion-inspired pet names, carrying French elegance and the timeless appeal of the little black dress. For the pet who always appears impeccably groomed, Coco provides fashion royalty. Versace brings Italian luxury and bold pattern. Armani suggests understated Italian elegance. Gucci carries recognizable luxury branding. Prada evokes Milan sophistication.\"]}]\n37:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arapaima/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arapaima\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"44\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alpaca/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alpaca\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"54\",{\"href\":\"/animal/amazon-parrot/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Amazon Parrot\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"71\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alpaca-huacaya/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Huacaya Alpaca\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"93\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alpine-salamander/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alpine Salamander\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n38:[\"$\",\"p\",\"26\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For more distinctive fashion naming: Dior brings French haute couture. Givenchy channels Audrey Hepburn elegance. McQueen honors Alexander McQueen's dramatic, boundary-pushing creativity. Yves (Saint Laurent) provides simple elegance. These fashion names celebrate the designers who shaped how we present ourselves to the world, giving pets identities wrapped in the artistry of clothing, accessory, and personal style. A pet named Coco or Armani carries a touch of runway elegance into every dog park visit and veterinary waiting room.\"]}]\n39:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🌍 A Real-World Naming Story\"]}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"28\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Sometimes the best names come from the most unexpected places. Take Elena, a wildlife photographer who spent months observing mongolian-wild-horses in their natural habitat. When she finally adopted one as a pet, the name came naturally: 'Obsidian' — inspired by the volcanic rock formations where she first encountered the species. 'I didn't choose the name,' Elena recalls. 'The experience chose it for me.'\"]}]\n3b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"29\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"This story illustrates a deeper naming principle: the most meaningful names aren't always found in lists or generators. They emerge from lived experience — a memorable trip, a childhood memory, a favorite artwork, a piece of music that moved you. These names carry stories, and stories are what transform a simple label into a lifelong connection with your animal companion.\"]}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"30\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Discover more naming inspiration: \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"34\",{\"href\":\"/animal/sperm-whale/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Sperm Whale\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"49\",{\"href\":\"/animal/polish-lowland-sheepdog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Polish Lowland Sheepdog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"76\",{\"href\":\"/animal/northern-flicker/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Northern Flicker\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"96\",{\"href\":\"/animal/foxface-rabbitfish/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Foxface Rabbitfish\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"118\",{\"href\":\"/animal/english-springer-spaniel/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"English Springer Spaniel\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and hundreds more animal name generators at BestAnimalNames.com.\"]}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the most popular artist names for pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Frida, Monet, Picasso, Dali, and Matisse are the most popular visual artist pet names. For musicians, Mozart, Beethoven, Bowie, and Ella dominate. These names carry recognizable cultural significance while remaining phonetically appealing for daily pet use.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do artistic names work for any pet species?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Artistic names transcend species. A hamster named Frida or a rabbit named Mozart carries the same cultural weight as a dog or cat with the same name. The perceived personality of different species even enhances certain names. Cats especially suit painter names for their natural grace.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I choose an artist name based on my pet's appearance or personality?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Both approaches work. Appearance matching like naming a blue-grey dog Picasso after his Blue Period creates visual-artistic connection. Personality matching like naming a dramatic pet Calliope for the dramatic muse rewards knowing your pet. The best artistic names often combine both elements.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I use lesser-known artists for truly unique pet names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Lesser-known artists provide the most unique names. Artemisia (Gentileschi, Baroque painter), Hilma (af Klint, abstract pioneer), and Basquiat (Jean-Michel, neo-expressionist) reward cultural knowledge while ensuring your pet's name stands out at every veterinary visit and dog park introduction.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What artistic names work well for pairs of pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Artistic pairs celebrate creative partnerships: Frida and Diego, John and Yoko, Gertrude and Alice, Pablo and Dora, Jackson and Lee. Famous artistic couples and collaborations provide meaningful paired naming that tells a story about creative partnership through your pets' companionship.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I choose between a music-inspired name and a visual-art-inspired name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Consider your pet's personality. Visual, observant pets who study their surroundings suit painter or sculptor names (Monet, Frida, Brancusi). Vocal, sound-responsive pets pair naturally with musical names (Jazz, Lyric, Cadence). Let your pet's natural tendencies guide you toward the right artistic discipline.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"dog\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐕\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Dog\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"cat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐱\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"parrot\",{\"href\":\"/animal/parrot/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦜\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Parrot\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"horse\",{\"href\":\"/animal/horse/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐴\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Horse\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"rabbit\",{\"href\":\"/animal/rabbit/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐰\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Rabbit\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"bird\",{\"href\":\"/animal/bird/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐦\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Bird\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"siamese-crocodile\",{\"href\":\"/animal/siamese-crocodile/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐊\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Siamese Crocodile\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"skunk-clownfish\",{\"href\":\"/animal/skunk-clownfish/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐠\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Skunk Clownfish\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"anoa\",{\"href\":\"/animal/anoa/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐃\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Anoa\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"tiger-shark\",{\"href\":\"/animal/tiger-shark/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦈\"}],\"$L43\"]}],\"$L44\"]}]]}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📖 Related Naming Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3\",\"children\":[null,null,null,[\"$\",\